Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:41:22 +0100
Forwarded: https://github.com/automataIA/onnx-vulkan-rs/pull/5
Subject: [PATCH] feat(core): Pad modes edge, reflect and wrap

Pad claimed nodes in any mode but ran only "constant"; a node in another
mode failed at run time, which ends hosts such as sherpa-onnx (Supertonic's
text encoder pads with "edge"). The device kernel (f32) and the host path
now map each output index to its source in all four modes, including pads
wider than the dimension and negative pads. A mode the kernel lacks and the
opset 18 "axes" input are refused at load time, so the node goes to another
provider. An empty dimension padded in a source mode is an error, not a crash.

Tested on a GTX 1060 (NVIDIA Vulkan) against numpy's np.pad.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
